      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-134876",
      ":question/problem": "Sophie wants to do at least $5$ math exercises in less than $48$ minutes. Let $x$ be the number of algebra exercises and $y$ the number of geometry exercises she does.\n\nWhich of the following shaded regions represents all possible combinations $(x, y)$ in which Sophie can do her exercises if she takes $8$ minutes to do an algebra exercise and $6$ minutes for a geometry exercise?\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
