      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-26551",
      ":question/problem": "An artist sells small paintings for $$300$ and large paintings for $$600$. Let $x$ be the number of small paintings and $y$ be the number of large paintings the artist sells.\n\nWhich of the following shaded regions represents all possible combinations $(x, y)$ in which the artist can sell his artwork if he wishes to make a profit of at least $$2400$ but he can make a maximum of $10$ paintings?\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
    }
